<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyrus the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">acceded 559 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Cyrus II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyrus the Great, or Cyrus II, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, who acceded in 559 BCE as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a>. He overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a>, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus of Lydia</a> and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in 539 BCE, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>. His policy of absorbing existing political and religious traditions, including Elamite ones, became a model for Persian rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great.jpg" alt="Cyrus the Great" width="261" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Surenae · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cyrus_II_(The_Great)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
